---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
---
<Layout title="About — Solomzi">
  <div class="wrap">
    <section class="hero" style="padding-bottom: 24px;">
      <div style="display:flex; align-items:center; gap:20px; flex-wrap:wrap; margin-bottom: 8px;">
        <svg width="88" height="88" viewBox="0 0 160 160" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" style="flex-shrink:0;">
          <style>
            .avatar-ping { animation: avatar-ping 2s ease-out infinite; transform-origin: 128px 128px; }
            .avatar-dot { animation: avatar-pulse 2s ease-out infinite; }
            @keyframes avatar-ping { 0% { r: 6; opacity: 0.6; } 100% { r: 17; opacity: 0; } }
            @keyframes avatar-pulse { 0%, 100% { opacity: 1; } 50% { opacity: 0.45; } }
            @media (prefers-reduced-motion: reduce) {
              .avatar-ping, .avatar-dot { animation: none; }
            }
          </style>
          <rect x="4" y="4" width="152" height="152" rx="24" fill="#1c2733" stroke="#2e3d4d" stroke-width="2" />
          <text x="80" y="98" font-family="monospace" font-size="52" font-weight="600" fill="#e8a33d" text-anchor="middle">&gt;_</text>
          <circle class="avatar-ping" cx="128" cy="128" r="6" fill="#5fb3a3" opacity="0.6" />
          <circle class="avatar-dot" cx="128" cy="128" r="7" fill="#5fb3a3" />
        </svg>
        <div>
          <span class="eyebrow">whoami</span>
          <h1 aria-label="About me" style="margin:0;">
            <span class="type-target" aria-hidden="true">About me</span><span class="caret" aria-hidden="true"></span>
          </h1>
        </div>
      </div>
      <p>
        IT Support Technician, Systems Administrator, and Network Engineer —
        self-taught into networking off the back of a Windows 98 PC and a lot
        of curiosity. Full story below, or just download the CV below.
      </p>
      <div class="hero-links">
        <a class="btn primary" href="/resume.pdf" download>Download CV</a>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="section" style="border-top: none;">
      <div class="section-label">// how i got here</div>
      <p style="color: var(--text); max-width: 68ch;">
        I first touched a computer at six years old, over a school holiday
        at my mom's house — one of those old white Windows 98 machines with
        a ball mouse. I spent the whole month trying to figure it out,
        mostly living in MS Paint because I used to be good at drawing. A couple of years
        later my primary school built a computer lab, here I took a computer class and learned the basics:
        what a computer actually is, software vs. hardware. I still remember the definition of a computer they gave us;
        "A computer is an electronic device that uses hardware and software" lol.
      </p>
      <p style="color: var(--text); max-width: 68ch;">
        When I was around 13, my mom bought me my own PC — a Pentium 4. I
        got into gaming hard: Max Payne, GTA, a lot of FPS games. That's
        what got me thinking I wanted to make games too, and I
        started looking into game design.
      </p>
      <p style="color: var(--text); max-width: 68ch;">
        By the time I applied for college at 17, the programming
        course I wanted was full, so I ended up in a Networking & PC
        Engineering course instead. Around then, a neighbor who turned out
        to be a network engineer had me over at his place, and I saw him running Packet
        Tracer, studying for his CCNA at the time. I was fascinated, but my head was
        still on game dev. Then first-year of college, C programming happened — badly
        taught, and it left me with a real phobia of code. But the
        following networking class flipped something: learning how routers
        and switches actually worked blew my mind. I went home, downloaded
        Packet Tracer, and started labbing constantly. The semester after
        that, a cybersecurity course introduced me to Linux, and I fell in
        even deeper.
      </p>
      <p style="color: var(--text); max-width: 68ch;">
        From there I was mostly self-taught — reading on my own, YouTube,
        endless labs, building VMs and servers just to see how things
        worked. School became more of a formality for the diploma than
        where the actual learning happened. I taught myself some pentesting,
        Python, and a bit of web dev along the way, self-studied my way to
        CCNA, and I'm working on CCNP now.
      </p>
      <p style="color: var(--text); max-width: 68ch;">
          What I actually love about this work is the troubleshooting — the
          journey of figuring something out, not just the fix itself. I've
          told my girlfriend more than once that there's a small thrill in
          typing <code>ping 1.2.3.4</code> and watching it come back clean.
          That's the job, distilled.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="section">
      <div class="section-label">// off the clock</div>
      <div class="skills-grid">
        <div class="skill-card">
          <div class="name">League of Legends</div>
          <div class="detail">Play a lot, watch a lot of esports too</div>
        </div>
        <div class="skill-card">
          <div class="name">Football &amp; F1</div>
          <div class="detail">Regular watcher of both</div>
        </div>
        <div class="skill-card">
          <div class="name">Cricket</div>
          <div class="detail">Team captain, back in high school</div>
        </div>
        <div class="skill-card">
          <div class="name">Gym</div>
          <div class="detail">Staying consistent</div>
        </div>
        <div class="skill-card">
          <div class="name">Manga &amp; Anime</div>
          <div class="detail">Regular reader/watcher</div>
        </div>
        <div class="skill-card">
          <div class="name">Music</div>
          <div class="detail">Pretty much always on</div>
        </div>
        <div class="skill-card">
        <div class="name">Learning German</div>
            <div class="detail">Work in progress</div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="section">
      <div class="section-label">// technical skills</div>
      <div class="skills-grid">
        <div class="skill-card">
          <div class="name">Systems &amp; Support</div>
          <div class="detail">Active Directory · Microsoft 365 · Entra ID · Windows/Linux/macOS</div>
        </div>
        <div class="skill-card">
          <div class="name">Networking</div>
          <div class="detail">TCP/IP · VLANs · BGP · OSPF · EIGRP · MPLS · VPNs (IPsec/OpenVPN)</div>
        </div>
        <div class="skill-card">
          <div class="name">Security</div>
          <div class="detail">Palo Alto · Fortinet · Cisco ASA · IDS/IPS · Zero Trust</div>
        </div>
        <div class="skill-card">
          <div class="name">Cloud</div>
          <div class="detail">Azure (VMs, Load Balancer, VNets, NSGs) · AWS · GCP</div>
        </div>
        <div class="skill-card">
          <div class="name">Automation &amp; Scripting</div>
          <div class="detail">Python · PowerShell · Bash · Ansible · Docker · Git</div>
        </div>
        <div class="skill-card">
          <div class="name">Monitoring &amp; Tools</div>
          <div class="detail">SolarWinds · Nagios · Splunk · Wireshark</div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="section">
      <div class="section-label">// experience</div>

      <div style="margin-bottom: 32px;">
        <div style="display:flex; justify-content:space-between; flex-wrap:wrap; gap:8px;">
          <strong style="color: var(--heading); font-size: 1.05rem;">IT Support Technician / Network &amp; Security Engineer</strong>
          <span class="mono" style="color: var(--text-dim); font-size: 0.85rem;">Jan 2024 – Present</span>
        </div>
        <div style="color: var(--text-dim); font-size: 0.9rem; margin-bottom: 10px;">ByteHub Solutions · Pretoria, South Africa</div>
        <ul style="color: var(--text); padding-left: 1.2em; margin: 0;">
          <li>Provide on-site and remote Level 1-2 support across Windows, Linux, and macOS; manage Microsoft 365, Entra ID, and Active Directory user accounts and access.</li>
          <li>Design and maintain multi-site hybrid network architecture across Azure, AWS, and on-prem infrastructure.</li>
          <li>Deploy firewall policies, IPsec/OpenVPN tunnels, ACLs, and Azure Load Balancer for secure, available applications.</li>
          <li>Install and maintain IP CCTV/NVR systems across hotel environments, diagnosing VLAN, PoE, and DHCP conflicts.</li>
          <li>Automate network configuration with Ansible and Python, cutting manual effort and config drift.</li>
          <li>Monitor network health and security posture with SolarWinds and Splunk; lead root cause analysis following ITIL process.</li>
        </ul>
      </div>

      <div>
        <div style="display:flex; justify-content:space-between; flex-wrap:wrap; gap:8px;">
          <strong style="color: var(--heading); font-size: 1.05rem;">Network &amp; IT Technician</strong>
          <span class="mono" style="color: var(--text-dim); font-size: 0.85rem;">Jan 2019 – Dec 2023</span>
        </div>
        <div style="color: var(--text-dim); font-size: 0.9rem; margin-bottom: 10px;">LTE Systems · Bulawayo, Zimbabwe</div>
        <ul style="color: var(--text); padding-left: 1.2em; margin: 0;">
          <li>Provided network and IT support across Cisco-based LAN/WAN infrastructure; administered switches, routers, and firewalls.</li>
          <li>Led migration from RIPv2 to OSPF, improving convergence and routing efficiency org-wide.</li>
          <li>Implemented and tuned Palo Alto and Fortinet next-gen firewalls, cutting security incidents by 75%.</li>
          <li>Designed VLANs and IPsec VPN topologies enforcing least-privilege segmentation across sites.</li>
          <li>Used Wireshark, Nagios, and Linux CLI for deep-packet analysis, log review, and incident response.</li>
        </ul>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="section">
      <div class="section-label">// certifications</div>
      <div class="skills-grid">
        <div class="skill-card">
          <div class="name">CCNP</div>
          <div class="detail">In progress · 2026</div>
        </div>
        <div class="skill-card">
          <div class="name">CCNA</div>
          <div class="detail">Dec 2022</div>
        </div>
        <div class="skill-card">
          <div class="name">Certified in Cybersecurity</div>
          <div class="detail">ISC2 · Jun 2023</div>
        </div>
        <div class="skill-card">
          <div class="name">Google Cybersecurity</div>
          <div class="detail">Professional Cert · Jun 2023</div>
        </div>
      </div>
      <p style="color: var(--text-dim); font-size: 0.9rem; margin-top: 16px;">
        Diploma in Networking &amp; PC Engineering — Midlands State University, Bulawayo · Nov 2021
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="section">
      <div class="section-label">// home lab &amp; projects</div>
      <svg viewBox="0 0 680 420" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="100%" role="img" style="max-width: 640px; margin-bottom: 24px;">
        <title>Home lab network topology</title>
        <desc>Internet connects to a firewall, which connects to a core switch, which distributes to three VLANs: Management, Servers and Lab, and Guest and IoT.</desc>
        <defs>
          <marker id="topo-arrow" viewBox="0 0 10 10" refX="8" refY="5" markerWidth="6" markerHeight="6" orient="auto-start-reverse">
            <path d="M2 1L8 5L2 9" fill="none" stroke="#5fb3a3" stroke-width="1.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" />
          </marker>
        </defs>
        <text x="340" y="24" text-anchor="middle" font-family="monospace" font-size="12" fill="#7d8b98">home lab topology</text>
        <circle cx="340" cy="55" r="18" fill="none" stroke="#2e3d4d" stroke-width="1.5" />
        <text x="340" y="59" text-anchor="middle" font-family="monospace" font-size="11" fill="#c8d0d8">WAN</text>
        <line x1="340" y1="73" x2="340" y2="100" stroke="#5fb3a3" stroke-width="1.5" marker-end="url(#topo-arrow)" />
        <rect x="260" y="100" width="160" height="46" rx="6" fill="#1c2733" stroke="#e8a33d" stroke-width="1.5" />
        <text x="340" y="119" text-anchor="middle" font-family="monospace" font-size="13" fill="#f2f5f7" font-weight="600">Firewall</text>
        <text x="340" y="135" text-anchor="middle" font-family="monospace" font-size="10" fill="#7d8b98">Fortinet / pfSense</text>
        <line x1="340" y1="146" x2="340" y2="173" stroke="#5fb3a3" stroke-width="1.5" marker-end="url(#topo-arrow)" />
        <rect x="250" y="173" width="180" height="46" rx="6" fill="#1c2733" stroke="#2e3d4d" stroke-width="1.5" />
        <text x="340" y="192" text-anchor="middle" font-family="monospace" font-size="13" fill="#f2f5f7" font-weight="600">Core switch</text>
        <text x="340" y="208" text-anchor="middle" font-family="monospace" font-size="10" fill="#7d8b98">802.1Q trunk</text>
        <line x1="340" y1="219" x2="130" y2="255" stroke="#2e3d4d" stroke-width="1.5" marker-end="url(#topo-arrow)" />
        <line x1="340" y1="219" x2="340" y2="255" stroke="#2e3d4d" stroke-width="1.5" marker-end="url(#topo-arrow)" />
        <line x1="340" y1="219" x2="550" y2="255" stroke="#2e3d4d" stroke-width="1.5" marker-end="url(#topo-arrow)" />
        <rect x="40" y="255" width="180" height="140" rx="8" fill="none" stroke="#2e3d4d" stroke-width="1" stroke-dasharray="4 3" />
        <text x="130" y="275" text-anchor="middle" font-family="monospace" font-size="11" fill="#5fb3a3" font-weight="600">VLAN 10 · Management</text>
        <rect x="60" y="290" width="140" height="34" rx="4" fill="#1c2733" stroke="#2e3d4d" stroke-width="1" />
        <text x="130" y="311" text-anchor="middle" font-family="monospace" font-size="11" fill="#c8d0d8">Switch mgmt / AP</text>
        <rect x="60" y="334" width="140" height="34" rx="4" fill="#1c2733" stroke="#2e3d4d" stroke-width="1" />
        <text x="130" y="355" text-anchor="middle" font-family="monospace" font-size="11" fill="#c8d0d8">Jump host</text>
        <rect x="250" y="255" width="180" height="140" rx="8" fill="none" stroke="#2e3d4d" stroke-width="1" stroke-dasharray="4 3" />
        <text x="340" y="275" text-anchor="middle" font-family="monospace" font-size="11" fill="#5fb3a3" font-weight="600">VLAN 20 · Servers &amp; lab</text>
        <rect x="270" y="290" width="140" height="34" rx="4" fill="#1c2733" stroke="#2e3d4d" stroke-width="1" />
        <text x="340" y="311" text-anchor="middle" font-family="monospace" font-size="11" fill="#c8d0d8">ESXi / Proxmox host</text>
        <rect x="270" y="334" width="140" height="34" rx="4" fill="#1c2733" stroke="#2e3d4d" stroke-width="1" />
        <text x="340" y="355" text-anchor="middle" font-family="monospace" font-size="11" fill="#c8d0d8">GNS3 / Docker labs</text>
        <rect x="460" y="255" width="180" height="140" rx="8" fill="none" stroke="#2e3d4d" stroke-width="1" stroke-dasharray="4 3" />
        <text x="550" y="275" text-anchor="middle" font-family="monospace" font-size="11" fill="#5fb3a3" font-weight="600">VLAN 30 · Guest &amp; IoT</text>
        <rect x="480" y="290" width="140" height="34" rx="4" fill="#1c2733" stroke="#2e3d4d" stroke-width="1" />
        <text x="550" y="311" text-anchor="middle" font-family="monospace" font-size="11" fill="#c8d0d8">CCTV / NVR</text>
        <rect x="480" y="334" width="140" height="34" rx="4" fill="#1c2733" stroke="#2e3d4d" stroke-width="1" />
        <text x="550" y="355" text-anchor="middle" font-family="monospace" font-size="11" fill="#c8d0d8">Guest Wi-Fi</text>
      </svg>
      <div class="skills-grid">
        <div class="skill-card">
          <div class="name">Enterprise Network Simulation</div>
          <div class="detail">BGP, OSPF, EIGRP, VLANs, STP, NAT, HSRP, monitoring — <a href="https://github.com/Ghostwolf73">GitHub</a></div>
        </div>
        <div class="skill-card">
          <div class="name">Routing &amp; VLAN Automation</div>
          <div class="detail">Ansible playbooks for BGP, OSPF, MPLS, VRF — <a href="https://github.com/Ghostwolf73/Routing_ansible">GitHub</a></div>
        </div>
        <div class="skill-card">
          <div class="name">DDoS Simulation &amp; Defence</div>
          <div class="detail">Python/Docker botnet sim + Ansible mitigation — <a href="https://github.com/Ghostwolf73/DDOS_script">GitHub</a></div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>
  </div>
</Layout>
